    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined by **Lawrence Butler**, whose matchup against Mitch Keller yields an elite score of 74.57. Benefitting from a +10% park factor and a +13% platoon edge, **Lawrence Butler** is our highest-projected source of counting stats today. **Bryson Stott** (70.11) and **Luis Arraez** (67.61) also anchor the daily output; **Bryson Stott** benefits from a favorable matchup against Phillips, while **Luis Arraez** capitalizes on the prime leadoff spot against the hittable G. Holmes. **Matt Chapman** rounds out our core recommendations, riding a strong +7% dynamic platoon advantage to a 65.85 score.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup today involved **Masyn Winn**, who sits at 50.66, narrowly edging out **Jeremiah Jackson** (38.29) for the final spot. While **Masyn Winn** provides elite speed\u2014a priority for our 5x5 build\u2014his matchup against M. King is suboptimal, and his score was hampered by a -2% penalty for the difficulty of the opposing arm. **Jeremiah Jackson** was the primary consideration for the bench, but his score cratered due to the L. Gilbert matchup and an assumed bottom-of-the-order assignment. We remain cautious with **Taylor Ward**, whose score of 40.87 reflects a high-risk matchup against the elite L. Gilbert; if the lineup confirms him lower than the leadoff spot, his efficiency score will likely plummet further. We continue to monitor the status of **Jonathan Aranda**, who is a \"Lineup Pending\" play; should he be omitted from the official card, we will need to pivot to preserve our game caps.",
